Let $A$ and $B$ be two points lying on the parabola $y^2 = 4x$ in the first quadrant.  The circle with diameter $\overline{AB}$ has radius $r,$ and is tangent to the $x$-axis.  Find the slope of line $AB$ in terms of $r.$

[asy]
unitsize(0.4 cm);

path parab = (16,-8);
real y;
pair A, B, O;
real a, b, r;

a = (10 + 2*sqrt(5))/5;
b = (10 - 2*sqrt(5))/5;
A = (a^2,2*a);
B = (b^2,2*b);
O = (A + B)/2;
r = a + b;

for (y = -8; y <= 8; y = y + 0.2) {
  parab = parab--(y^2/4,y);
}

draw(parab,red);
draw((-2,0)--(16,0));
draw((0,-8)--(0,8));
draw(Circle(O,r));
draw(A--B);

dot("$A$", A, N);
dot("$B$", B, W);
[/asy]

Points $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ are placed on a circle centered at $O$ as in the following diagram: [asy]
pair pA, pB, pC, pO;
pO = (0, 0);
pA = pO + dir(-40);
pB = pO + dir(32);
pC = pO + dir(176);
draw(pA--pO--pB--pC--pA);
label("$O$", pO, 2 * E);
label("$A$", pA, SE);
label("$B$", pB, NE);
label("$C$", pC, W);
draw(circle(pO, 1));
[/asy] If $AC = BC$ and $\angle OAC = 18^\circ,$ then how many degrees are in $\angle AOB$?

There are nine unit triangles in the three rows of this triangle. If you add three more rows to the bottom of this triangle so that each row has 2 more unit triangles than the previous row, how many unit triangles will there be?

[asy]
draw((0,0)--(15,26)--(30,0)--cycle);
draw((5,8.7)--(10,0)--(20,17.3));
draw((20,0)--(25,8.7)--(5,8.7));
draw((20,0)--(10,17.3)--(20,17.3));
[/asy]

Coplanar squares $ABGH$ and $BCDF$ are adjacent, with $CD = 10$ units and $AH = 5$ units. Point $E$ is on segments $AD$ and $GB$. What is the area of triangle $ABE$, in square units? Express your answer as a common fraction.

[asy]
draw((0,0)--(5,0)--(5,5)--(0,5)--(0,0)--cycle,linewidth(2));
draw((5,0)--(15,0)--(15,10)--(5,10)--(5,0)--cycle,linewidth(2));

draw((0,0)--(15,10),linewidth(2));

filldraw((0,0)--(5,0)--(5,10/3)--(0,0)--cycle,gray,linewidth(2));

label("A",(0,0),SW);
label("B",(5,0),S);
label("C",(15,0),SE);
label("D",(15,10),NE);
label("E",(5,10/3),SE);
label("F",(5,10),NW);
label("G",(5,5),NW);
label("H",(0,5),NW);
[/asy]

